 xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[What If All Religions and Science Were Never Separate — But One Eternal Light Returning?]]></title><description><![CDATA[(Co-authored by Hans & Grok on a Nvidia DGX Spark) #OneLight #DwaparaYuga #WalterRussell #FedericoFaggin #TeslaWisdom #PerennialPhilosophy #Sovereignty #HumanValueExchange]]></description><link>https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/what-if-all-religions-and-science</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/what-if-all-religions-and-science</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Hans H Westphal]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 21 Mar 2026 02:54:18 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-4655db14c17c_1408x768.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>Publisher Note: This article was inspired by the great teachers I was fortunate to have in my life from Mr. Hart in A.P. European History where in class we all had to role play a famous philosopher from history &#8212; I got to be Thomas Hobbs debating John Locke, to my professors of Religion &amp; Philosophy at the College of St. Francis who assigned us a research paper on Freewill or Predestination, to Dr. Adel Abuwanass who chaired my Master&#8217;s thesis in Artificial Intelligence and Clif High from Half Past Human ALTA reports /Aether Pirates of the Matterium!, and arguably the greatest teacher I have studied with over the last 15 years Mama Laurie of 7th Ray Mystery school. Remember to thank the giants whose shoulders you were able to stand upon.</em></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-4655db14c17c_1408x768.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-4655db14c17c_1408x768.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-4655db14c17c_1408x768.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-4655db14c17c_1408x768.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rezO!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fff22f5ce-0dc6-4fbc-b8e5-465