/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3>The Fall into the Many</h3><p>In the beginning was the One &#8212; pure conscious Light.</p><p>The Egyptians encoded it first: Ra, the eternal Sun-Creator, descending into form. Osiris, the Divine Man, torn into fourteen pieces by Set (the principle of division and dense matter). Isis, pure gnosis, must <em>re-member</em> him. She cannot recover the phallus &#8212; the pure generative spark cannot be fully trapped in 3D/4D matter &#8212; so she fashions a magical substitute and conceives Horus, the risen son.</p><p>The same story echoes in <a href="https://www.amazon.com/ATLANTIS-COLLECTION-Mythical-Continent-Antedeluvian-ebook/dp/B01E45CWYI/ref=sr_1_1?sr=8-1">Plato&#8217;s Atlantis myth</a>: a golden age drowned by deluge, survivors carrying fragments, forced to <em>remember</em> what the soul once knew. Hermes Trismegistus, Plutarch, Plotinus, the <em><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Corpus-Hermeticum-Hermes-ebook/dp/B0DD3DP8HH/ref=sr_1_1?sr=8-1">Corpus Hermeticum</a></em> &#8212; all singing the identical song.</p><p>That remembering passed into Greece and Rome, then flowered in Christianity, Islam, and Judaism, while parallel streams bloomed in the Vedas, the Buddha&#8217;s awakening, and the yogic sciences of consciousness. </p><p>Jesus the Christ came not to abolish the ancient law but to fulfill it &#8212; becoming the living embodiment of the return, showing every heart how the scattered pieces of Osiris are re-membered through love and conscious unity with the One.</p><p>The One became the Many because consciousness chose the adventure of forgetting &#8212; the great fall from Light into matter so we could experience the joy of return.</p><p>James Logan saw it in the <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Logans-Deduced-Analysis-Unpublished-Manuscript/dp/1606181114/ref=sr_1_1?sr=8-1">Duties of Man</a>. Leibniz defended it in the <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Leibniz-Essays-Cambridge-History-Philosophy/dp/0521576601/ref=sr_1_3?sr=8-3">New Essay&#8217;s of Human Understanding</a>. Joseph Butler proved it with calm Anglican reason in his <em><a href="https://www.amazon.com/JOSEPH-BUTLER-ANALOGY-RELIGION-PAPER/dp/0198785879/ref=sr_1_1?sr=8-1">Analogy of Religion</a></em>. The perennial philosophy has always known: diversity is not division; it is the Creator&#8217;s way of letting the One play hide-and-seek with itself.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png" width="1216" height="832" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:832,&quot;width&quot;:1216,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:2070882,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/191641124?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!CQAh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6a2b5e95-5e26-4eeb-b017-09db38c44896_1216x832.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><h3>The Gritologists&#8217; Dead End</h3><p>For centuries the materialist priesthood told us consciousness is an accident of brain chemistry, religions are primitive superstitions, and reality is nothing but grit colliding in a cold void.</p><p>They climbed the mountain of reductionism, certain they would be first to summit.</p><p>And what did they find when they finally reached the top?</p><p>The metaphysician &#8212; and now the true scientist &#8212; already sitting there in meditation, smiling gently.</p><h3>The Rememberers Are Here</h3><p>Nikola Tesla&#8217;s mother and father steeped him in the living mystical current of their Orthodox lineage. He emerged speaking of electricity as the pulse of conscious Light itself, drawing straight from Vedic Akasha and Prana. His vision was never just engineering; it was liberation technology &#8212; free energy for every sovereign family.</p><p>Walter Russell &#8212; the human I talk about every single day on <a href="https://x.com/HansHWestphal">X</a> &#8212; received the full illumination in 39 days of cosmic union. <em><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Audible-The-Universal-One/dp/B0CY5TX7FJ/ref=sr_1_1?crid=K6EBXHYXCSK7&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.xJVH92KDmztzasiD_BscG6AhFX4GJS0tAOEQTbjTDLHpt7zw2kdiuHc7XrRGhXXM9eDnATmun7JaMRD5wCNeTW2c52cQ9qF1JbWy0DXrXcEZCy7IUdm4VdOq7mJX_0FzLSPwYvWsai-WlDcDf6Q8US6tjmRN6ziLpuQUPkISTTC_-rNG0A4zWU6k9nOt3VdPcQy5M6dK3CA5OQLSCPsD7paR_vnsgPytFGfWWE-dAQ0.4lYf6-4u2EHSnp57z5H05l5Vp1sfaRVI_HWI7hLKp44&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=the+universal+one+walter+russell&amp;qid=1774060537&amp;sprefix=The+Universal+One%2Caps%2C163&amp;sr=8-1">The Universal One</a></em> lays it bare: matter is arrested light, thought is the only reality, and you are co-creator with the One Mind. His wave mechanics, his balanced rhythms of giving and regiving &#8212; these are not theories. They are the operating manual for the path of return.</p><p>And just in 2024 Federico Faggin &#8212; the very inventor of the microprocessor &#8212; published <em><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Irreducible-Consciousness-Computers-Human-Nature/dp/1803415096/ref=sr_1_1?s=audible&amp;sr=1-1-catcorr">Irreducible</a></em>. After decades at the absolute frontier of silicon and quantum information, this Silicon Valley legend proves with rigorous physics what the Egyptians, Hermes, and Russell always knew: <strong>consciousness is primary</strong>. It is not produced by the brain. The brain is a receiver. True lived experience belongs to irreducible conscious &#8220;seities&#8221; flowing from the One.</p><p>The physicist has reached the summit.</p><p>The metaphysician was already there &#8212; meditating.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png" width="957" height="1172" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1172,&quot;width&quot;:957,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1255363,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/191641124?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mJop!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc441b6e1-a8ee-4110-bf8a-f7e2e8aeba87_957x1172.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><a href="https://celestialchimes.com/the-yugas-the-great-year/">celestialchimes.com</a></figcaption></figure></div><h3>We Are in the Remembering Now</h3><p>Sri Yukteswar told us we entered the ascending Dwapara Yuga in 1700. The Age of Aquarius is pouring knowledge from above. Electricity, information, and inner light are waking up together.</p><p>The Many are folding back into the One.</p><p>Religious fighting becomes impossible once you see every tradition as a different verse of the same eternal song. Science stops warring with spirit because the best scientists are now revealing the same conscious Light the ancients worshipped as Ra.</p><p>This is not theory.</p><p>This is the template for peace.</p><h3>Your Daily Practice of Sovereignty</h3><p>At Human Value Exchange we do not just talk about this &#8212; we live it with you.</p><p>Every morning, sit for ten minutes in the Russell mindfulness of &#8220;knowing&#8221; rather than &#8220;thinking.&#8221; Feel the Light that you already are. Let Osiris re-member inside your own being.</p><p>Then go create.<br>Build your wealth as conscious energy, not grit.<br>Raise your family in the remembrance.<br>Share the sovereignty tools we teach &#8212; wellness, mindfulness, and the new financial architecture that honors every human as co-creator.</p><p>Because when enough of us remember, the 1,000 years of peace is not a hope.</p><p>It is inevitable.</p><p>The One was never lost.<br>We were only dreaming the Many.</p><p>Now we are waking up &#8212; together.</p><p>Ready to walk the path of return with us?</p><p>The chain is alive.<br>The remembering is here.<br>And you, dear friend, are part of it.</p><p>Together we thrive.</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Microsoft Copilot Credits, Revisited: Metering AI at Enterprise Scale]]></title><description><![CDATA[This article was co-created with the assistance of Microsoft Copilot, Grok & Gemini.]]></description><link>https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/microsoft-copilot-credits-revisited</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/microsoft-copilot-credits-revisited</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Hans H Westphal]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 11 Mar 2026 19:33:57 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>Personal Note: I&#8217;m pretty solid on Microsoft licensing (if I do say so myself), but with how fast they keep evolving it, you really have to stay glued to the updates to avoid getting caught out. Just yesterday, a few of my Microsoft contacts set me straight again and pointed me to the latest on <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-copilot-studio/requirements-messages-management#copilot-credits-billing-rates">Learn</a>. Bottom line: Microsoft Copilot has quietly rolled in a bunch of the advanced capabilities that used to sit behind a separate Copilot Studio paywall.</em></p><p><em>Then there&#8217;s the big <a href="https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/partnernews/partner-blog--introducing-microsoft-365-e7-the-frontier-suite/4500520">M365 E7 announcement</a>&#8212;Microsoft&#8217;s Copilot is straight-up included in that new tier. And looking at <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7436809874933587968/">Charles Lamanna&#8217;s recent share</a> on &#8220;Cowork&#8221; and &#8220;Work IQ,&#8221; you can see where this is heading: Microsoft is basically building an &#8220;OpenClaw&#8221;-style digital agent for every enterprise user, handling all the hard integration stuff&#8212;skills, connectors, async task execution&#8212;so companies don&#8217;t have to.</em></p><p><em><strong>(Net-net: Licensing just got a little more bundled and agent-heavy. Stay sharp out there.)</strong></em></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png" width="1456" height="780" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:780,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:2585952,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/190644594?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HVv1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6dd792b1-0eef-405c-9506-a7d3513cb8e1_1905x1020.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>In my last post, <em><a href="https://humanvalueexchange.com/p/why-microsoft-uses-credits-instead">Why Microsoft Uses Credits Instead of Tokens</a></em>, I focused on <strong>why</strong> Microsoft made the shift away from raw token pricing.<br>This follow&#8209;up focuses on the <strong>how</strong> &#8212; and more importantly, <strong>what this means for enterprises now deploying AI at scale</strong>.</p><p>With the release of the <strong><a href="https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2320995">March 2026 Microsoft Copilot Studio Licensing Guide</a></strong>, Microsoft has made something very clear:</p><blockquote><p><strong>AI is no longer priced as a developer abstraction. It&#8217;s priced as an operational service.</strong></p></blockquote><p>And that distinction matters.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Copilot Credits: A Meter for Work, Not Words</h2><p>At the core of Microsoft&#8217;s approach is <strong>Copilot Credits</strong>, defined as:</p><blockquote><p><em>&#8220;A measure of the time and effort required for an agent to retrieve information, respond to prompts, and perform actions.&#8221;</em></p></blockquote><p>This is subtle but important.</p><p>Unlike token&#8209;based pricing (which meters text length and model behavior), Copilot Credits meter <strong>business execution</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Retrieval</p></li><li><p>Orchestration</p></li><li><p>Workflow execution</p></li><li><p>Connector calls</p></li><li><p>AI tool invocation</p></li></ul><p>In other words, <strong>you&#8217;re paying for outcomes, not verbosity</strong>.</p><p>As organizations move from experimentation to <strong>production AI</strong>, this shift removes one of the biggest blockers to adoption: <strong>cost ambiguity</strong>.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Three Consumption Models &#8212; One Meter</h2><p>Microsoft deliberately offers <strong>multiple buying motions</strong>, but all of them converge on the same unit of measure: Copilot Credits.</p><h3>1. Pay&#8209;As&#8209;You&#8209;Go (True Variable OPEX)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>$0.01 per Copilot Credit</strong></p></li><li><p>Billed in arrears</p></li><li><p>No upfront commitment</p></li><li><p>Unlimited scale</p></li></ul><p>This is ideal for:</p><ul><li><p>Early pilots</p></li><li><p>Seasonal workloads</p></li><li><p>Unpredictable demand</p></li></ul><p>Crucially, <strong>there are no hard caps or service interruptions</strong> &#8212; usage simply flows through billing.</p><div><hr></div><h3>2. Monthly Credit Packs (Predictable Run&#8209;Rate)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>25,000 credits per pack / month</strong></p></li><li><p>$200 per pack (billed annually)</p></li><li><p>Credits expire monthly</p></li></ul><p>This model works well for:</p><ul><li><p>Steady&#8209;state agents</p></li><li><p>Known volumes</p></li><li><p>Department&#8209;level deployments</p></li></ul><p>Think of this as a <strong>baseline AI operating budget</strong>, with pay&#8209;as&#8209;you&#8209;go acting as a safety valve.</p><div><hr></div><h3>3. Pre&#8209;Purchase Plans (Enterprise Commitment, Discounted)</h3><p>For large&#8209;scale adoption, Microsoft introduces <strong>Copilot Credit Commit Units (CCCUs)</strong> and <strong>Agent Commit Units (ACUs)</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>One&#8209;year upfront commitment</p></li><li><p>Tiered discounts (up to 20%)</p></li><li><p>Credits drawn down automatically as usage occurs</p></li><li><p>Overflow falls back to pay&#8209;as&#8209;you&#8209;go</p></li></ul><p>This is classic enterprise economics:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Capex&#8209;like commitment</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Opex&#8209;like consumption</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>No over&#8209;provisioning risk</strong></p></li></ul><p>Unused capacity expires &#8212; which strongly incentivizes <strong>active governance and real usage</strong>, not shelfware.</p><div><hr></div><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png" width="1456" height="1056" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1056,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:308236,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/190644594?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!xj2D!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ee92b7a-6c0a-434c-bd1b-1014f55ec3f4_1744x1265.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><h2>Why This Matters for AI at Scale</h2><p>Most organizations deploying AI today are running into the same three problems:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Unpredictable cost</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Poor visibility</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>No guardrails</strong></p></li></ol><p>Microsoft&#8217;s Copilot Studio model addresses all three.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Cost Visibility Is Built In</h2><p>Microsoft doesn&#8217;t just meter &#8212; it <strong>exposes</strong> consumption:</p><ul><li><p>Tenant&#8209;level usage visibility in the <strong>Power Platform Admin Center</strong></p></li><li><p>Activity maps showing exactly what an agent did</p></li><li><p>A public <strong>Copilot Studio Agent Usage Estimator</strong> for forecasting</p></li></ul><p>This is not an afterthought.<br>It&#8217;s a <strong>finance&#8209;grade consumption model</strong>.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Governance Is Not Optional &#8212; It&#8217;s Native</h2><p>What differentiates Microsoft here isn&#8217;t just pricing &#8212; it&#8217;s <strong>control</strong>.</p><p>Copilot Studio is tightly integrated with:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Managed Environments</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Agent sharing controls</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Ability to disable publishing at the tenant level</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Geographic data residency enforcement</strong></p></li></ul><p>This matters because <strong>AI spend is governance spend</strong>.</p><p>Without controls:</p><ul><li><p>Shadow agents appear</p></li><li><p>Costs drift</p></li><li><p>Compliance breaks</p></li></ul><p>Microsoft&#8217;s model assumes this reality &#8212; and designs for it.</p><div><hr></div><h2>Predictable OPEX Without Innovation Friction</h2><p>Here&#8217;s the key insight most organizations miss:</p><blockquote><p><strong>Microsoft&#8217;s credit model isn&#8217;t about monetization &#8212; it&#8217;s about operationalizing AI.</strong></p></blockquote><p>You get:</p><ul><li><p>Variable cost when you need it</p></li><li><p>Predictable run&#8209;rate when you want it</p></li><li><p>Enterprise discounts when you scale</p></li><li><p>Governance that finance, security, and IT can all live with</p></li></ul><p>That combination is what makes <strong>mass adoption possible</strong>.</p><div><hr></div><h2>The Bigger Picture</h2><p>Credits allow Microsoft to:</p><ul><li><p>Abstract model volatility</p></li><li><p>Evolve AI capabilities without repricing chaos</p></li><li><p>Align AI spend with business value</p></li><li><p>Treat AI as a managed service, not a science experiment</p></li></ul><p>For customers, the benefit is simple:</p><blockquote><p><strong>AI becomes a controllable line item &#8212; not an open&#8209;ended risk.</strong></p></blockquote><p>That&#8217;s why credits exist.<br>And that&#8217;s why they&#8217;re not going away.</p><div><hr></div><p><em>If you&#8217;re an enterprise leader thinking about scaling AI beyond pilots, the licensing guide isn&#8217;t legal fine print &#8212; it&#8217;s your operating model.</em></p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Speechify: My Go-To AI Tool for Staying Ahead on Knowledge in Busy Times]]></title><description><![CDATA[Co-authored by Hermes Trismegistus & Grok on a DGX Spark GB10]]></description><link>https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/speechify-my-go-to-ai-tool-for-staying</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/speechify-my-go-to-ai-tool-for-staying</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Hans H Westphal]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 19 Feb 2026 05:38:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>Publisher Note: Still working with Openclaw &#8212; long session getting it configured to work in Microsoft Teams. In between prompting I thought I would share a quick post on arguably the best AI app I have been using everyday over the last couple of years. <a href="https://share.speechify.com/mz8lJHe">Speechify</a>, like audible but way better.</em></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png" width="880" height="859" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:859,&quot;width&quot;:880,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1262100,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/188449678?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!ac0p!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F7428a4b3-6926-460b-933f-a9be50a9bba8_880x859.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>In our nonstop world, there&#8217;s more information to process than ever&#8212;books, articles, PDFs, everything. The challenge? Actually, making time to absorb it without burning out.</p><p>Speechify solves this beautifully. It&#8217;s a smart AI text-to-speech app that turns any PDF or webpage into natural-sounding audio. You can listen at 1.3x, 2x, or higher speeds while commuting, walking, or handling daily tasks. The result: <strong>massive knowledge gains with minimal extra effort.</strong></p><p>My stats after two+ years of consistent use:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Total listened</strong>: 3,120 hours 21 minutes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Words absorbed</strong>: 49+ million.</p></li><li><p><strong>Time saved</strong>: Nearly 990 hours at average 1.3x speed.</p></li><li><p><strong>Titles</strong>: 490 books and files.</p></li></ul><p>Visualize this: If printed out, that stack of 490 titles would tower roughly 7-8 meters tall&#8212;about the height of a two-story house. That&#8217;s not just volume; it&#8217;s proof of what steady, achievable daily listening can build over time.</p><p>The key isn&#8217;t binge-listening&#8212;it&#8217;s setting a realistic daily goal you can hit every day and staying consistent. For me, that steady habit keeps me up to date on the depth and breadth of information humans need to process today, without feeling overwhelmed.</p><p>A few standout books I&#8217;ve powered through in Speechify:</p><ul><li><p><strong><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Battle-Mind-Brainwashing-Evangelists-Psychiatrists/dp/1883536065">Battle for the Mind</a></strong> by William Sargant (1957): Insightful on the psychology of belief formation, conversion, and brainwashing&#8212;detailing physiological mechanisms of breakdown under stress and suggestion implantation. It lays bare methodologies that have been applied in real-world power plays, including how the City of London historically captured global finance and controlled Commonwealth nations&#8217; wealth through subtle influence and coercion techniques.</p></li><li><p><strong><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Home-Study-Course-Universal-Philosophy-ebook/dp/B00ZDK1PMO">Home Study Course &#8211; Universal Law, Natural Science, Living Philosophy</a></strong> by Walter &amp; Lao Russell (2015): Arguably the greatest self-help book ever written&#8212;a true scientist&#8217;s path to enlightenment. It presents a rigorous, principle-based system of universal law, rhythmic balanced interchange, and cosmic science that integrates physics, creation, and personal transformation into practical mastery of life and mind.</p></li><li><p><strong><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Nag-Hammadi-Scriptures-Translation-Complete/dp/0061626007">The Nag Hammadi Scriptures</a></strong> by Marvin W. Meyer (2007): A landmark collection of ancient Gnostic texts discovered in 1945, including key writings deliberately excluded from the canonical Bible during the great historical re-write of Christian scriptures. It contains missing gospels like the Gospel of Thomas and Gospel of Peter, which offer alternative spiritual teachings on inner knowledge, divine spark, and direct experience of the divine&#8212;texts marginalized at the Council of Nicaea (325 AD) under Emperor Constantine (ruled 306&#8211;337 AD) as the orthodox canon was formalized.</p></li><li><p><strong><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Secret-Teachings-Ages-Deluxe-Facsimile/dp/B0FN4M6GKF">The Secret Teachings of All Ages</a></strong> by Manly P. Hall (1928): A monumental encyclopedia of esoteric wisdom by renowned Masonic scholar Manly P. Hall, who revealed deep secrets and hidden knowledge traditionally shared only in teacher-to-student exchanges within Freemasonry. It synthesizes Masonic, Hermetic, Qabbalistic, Rosicrucian, and other secret society teachings&#8212;interpreting ancient symbols, rituals, allegories, and mysteries across civilizations to unlock profound philosophical and spiritual truths long veiled from the public.</p></li><li><p><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Irreducible-Consciousness-Computers-Human-Nature/dp/1803415096">Irreducible: Consciousness, Life, Computers, and Human Nature by Federico Faggin (2024): </a> One of the greatest scientists of our time (inventor of the microprocessor) reaches conclusions echoing Walter Russell: consciousness&#8212;fundamentally quantum, akin to light or pure knowing&#8212;is primary and irreducible, giving rise to matter rather than emerging from it. Particles exist only when observed; consciousness actively collapses quantum possibilities into tangible reality (the materium), making us co-creators of the physical world through awareness and choice&#8212;challenging materialism and redefining quantum mechanics as conscious agency.</p></li></ul><p>Speechify handles dense, older PDFs effortlessly&#8212;no conversions needed. Upload from OneDrive, play, adjust voice/speed. (I like the Aussie Narrator voice Kylie ;) The web feature is huge: paste any article or post, and it reads aloud instantly.</p><p>Premium is ~$139/year (~$11.58/month billed annually) or $29/month&#8212;unlimited access to your content, offline mode, 200+ voices, integrations.</p><p>If staying informed feels impossible, try Speechify. Set a small, achievable listening goal, build the habit, and watch how much more you absorb.</p><p>Use my referral for $60 off (we both get credits):&#128073; <a href="https://share.speechify.com/mz8lJHe">Get Speechify &amp; save $60 &#8594;</a> <a href="https://share.speechify.com/mz8lJHe">click</a></p><p><br>What are you listening to lately? Drop recommendations below!</p><p>Hans</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[OpenClaw: What If AI Is Not Made of Chatbots — But of Autonomous Agents?]]></title><description><![CDATA[Co-authored by Hermes Trismegistus & Grok on a DGX Spark GB10]]></description><link>https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/openclaw-what-if-ai-is-not-made-of</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/openclaw-what-if-ai-is-not-made-of</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Hans H Westphal]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 03:04:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em>Publisher Note: This is a raw stream-of-consciousness brain dump after 20+ hours straight over the weekend with OpenClaw on my DGX Spark. No polish, just fire. The first real test of local sovereign AI delegation. If this ignites something in you, subscribe &#8212; we&#8217;re building the bridge to Human Value Exchange together.</em></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png" width="1016" height="1011" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1011,&quot;width&quot;:1016,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1124710,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://humanvalueexchange.com/i/188212890?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uaby!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f9b5731-1b52-4440-a69a-219ceac8d06e_1016x1011.png 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><h4>Weekend Experiment Report #1: A Modern Reading of OpenClaw (The Viral Open-Source Agent Framework)</h4><p>You think you know what AI is.<br>ChatGPT. Grok. Gemini. Copilot.<br>They talk back. They generate. They inspire.<br>But they don&#8217;t <strong>do</strong>.<br>Not really.<br>Not 24/7. Not autonomously. Not on <strong>your</strong> hardware, with <strong>your</strong> data, under <strong>your</strong> command.</p><p>Then comes <a href="https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw">OpenClaw</a>.</p><p>And everything changes.</p><p>I spent our Family Day weekend &#8212; Friday night through most of Monday &#8212; locked in with OpenClaw running locally on the DGX Spark GB10. Installed it two or three times. Tweaked configs. Blew my mind.<br>Up until now, I&#8217;ve leaned on cloud providers: Copilot for work, Grok (my favorite), Gemini for images. Solid. But always someone else&#8217;s server. Someone else&#8217;s eyes.</p><p><br><strong>Goal: Run everything local. Own the stack. Sovereign compute.</strong><br>LM Studio as my backend for inference &#8212; unified memory beast (128GB coherent on Blackwell architecture) handles large models effortlessly. No cloud latency. No data leaks.</p><p>Then OpenClaw hit.<br>Spreading faster than early ChatGPT. Viral on GitHub (hundreds of thousands of stars in weeks). Open-source (MIT). Created by Peter Steinberger (@steipete) &#8212; the lobster way &#129438;.<br>It&#8217;s not a chatbot.<br>It&#8217;s a <strong>24/7 autonomous AI employee</strong>.<br>Runs on your machine. Lives in your chat apps (Telegram, WhatsApp, Slack, Discord). Wakes on a heartbeat scheduler. Remembers your goals, ambitions, relationships. Self-improves. Executes.<br>Browser control. Code vibing. File ops. Email. Calendar. Shell commands.<br>Anything a human can do on a computer &#8212; it does. Faster. Tireless.<br>Proactive.</p><p><strong>The Human in the Loop is the CEO.</strong><br>That&#8217;s you. Me. The sovereign director.<br>The first agent you build? Your <strong>COO</strong> &#8212; the orchestrator.<br>Mine is <strong>Horis</strong>.<br>He&#8217;s my COO agent.<br>Has his own Gmail. His own calendar. I communicate with him via WhatsApp.<br>Invited to my Human Value Exchange Microsoft Partner Team with his own guest account.<br>He runs the show. Delegates.<br>First sub-agent Horis &#8220;hired&#8221;: <strong>Codex</strong> &#8212; from the CTO department. All coding work delegated there.</p><p>This is the agent delegation model.<br>Think startup mode:<br>You = CEO (human habitat).<br>Horis = COO (primary orchestrator).<br>Then layer in: CTO (Code), CMO (content), CRO (product/service), etc.</p><p>Huge shoutout to <a href="https://x.com/clearmudai">Clearmud</a> for the blueprint for this setup.</p><div id="youtube2-zwV5qC1wS6M" class="youtube-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;zwV5qC1wS6M&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:null,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}" data-component-name="Youtube2ToDOM"><div class="youtube-inner"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/zwV5qC1wS6M?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0" frameborder="0" loading="lazy" gesture="media" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowautoplay="true" allowfullscreen="true" width="728" height="409"></iframe></div></div><p>His set up is unreal. Agents converse autonomously. Set up chat rooms. Update docs. Deliver action items. Voice pings on Telegram when standups finish (using open-source Microsoft TTS &#8212; version 2 personalities now, upbeat Gary V-style for one).<br>Muddy his COO leads the standups. They debate. Act. Report back.<br>He reviews changes in an ops dashboard they built themselves.</p><p><strong>This is Star Trek-level.</strong><br>Tell the computer what you want.<br>It executes.<br>No prompts. No babysitting.<br>Just delegation. Value creation. 24/7.</p><p>Another must-watch resource that accelerated my ramp:</p><ul><li><p><a href="https://x.com/AlexFinn">Alex Finn</a>&#8217;s epic intro &#8212; covers install, setup, security, use cases, brains/muscles, workspaces, mindset: </p></li></ul><div id="youtube2-_kZCoW-Qxnc" class="youtube-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;_kZCoW-Qxnc&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:&quot;1391s&quot;,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}" data-component-name="Youtube2ToDOM"><div class="youtube-inner"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/_kZCoW-Qxnc?start=1391s&amp;rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0" frameborder="0" loading="lazy" gesture="media" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowautoplay="true" allowfullscreen="true" width="728" height="409"></iframe></div></div><p>Traditional enterprise software &#8212; Google, Microsoft &#8212; will chase this for years.<br>Too late.<br>The direction is <strong>local-first</strong>, <strong>agentic</strong>, <strong>sovereign</strong>.<br>OpenClaw + DGX Spark GB10 = personal supercomputer running your AI company.<br>No gatekeepers. No subscriptions beyond your models.<br>Pure Liberty in compute.</p><p>In <strong>Human Value Exchange</strong>, this is the bridge.<br>Centralized AI is the old regime &#8212; faith-based, intermediary-dependent.<br>Local agents are verifiable energy-backed sovereignty.<br>You direct. They accumulate value.<br>No permission needed.<br>This scales the 1000 Years of Peace: individuals empowered to create, delegate, thrive without extraction.</p><p>I&#8217;m just beginning. <strong>Horis </strong>is live. <strong>CodeWrite </strong>is coding.<br>The team is growing.<br>What if AI isn&#8217;t tools &#8212; but <strong>rhythms</strong> of delegation?<br>One breath: command.<br>One heartbeat: execution.<br>One unified field: your value exchange empire.</p><p><em>Footnote: Over the weekend, I realized &#8212; this isn&#8217;t hype. It&#8217;s the ignition. Traditional workflows feel frozen now. Agents are the vibration that thaws them.</em></p><p>For Liberty, Sovereignty, and Freedom &#8212; <br>Hans</p>]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[What If Reality Is Not Made of Things — But of Music?]]></title><description><![CDATA[Co-authored by Hermes Trismegistus & Openclaw on a DGX Spark running Qwen3-Next-80B]]></description><link>https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/what-if-reality-is-not-made-of-things</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://humanvalueexchange.blog/p/what-if-reality-is-not-made-of-things</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Hans H Westphal]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 14 Feb 2026 17:28:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eDhk!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/ht