4ceaf31-4701-44a2-a9c2-300d3a7ff28c_801x764.png 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>I learned the hard way during the Celsius collapse that &#8220;Not your keys, not your coins&#8221; isn&#8217;t just a slogan&#8212;it&#8217;s a survival rule. I trusted a custodial platform with my Bitcoin, and when Celsius went under, so did my funds. That loss drove home the importance of self-custody: if you don&#8217;t control your private keys, you don&#8217;t truly own your Bitcoin. For anyone serious about financial sovereignty, a non-custodial solution is essential. Bitcoin Well empowers you to buy, sell, and manage Bitcoin safely&#8212;without sacrificing ownership or security.</p><p>This partnership feels especially timely given Adam O&#8217;Brien&#8217;s inspiring <a href="https://x.com/adamobrien/status/2009398982301372436?s=20">New Year&#8217;s resolution talk</a>.  Adam and I are deeply aligned: both of us are building sovereignty across North America through self-custody, node-running, community amplification, and circular economies. His call to action &#8212; take self-custody now, run a personal node for verification and privacy, and amplify through local meetups and merchant adoption &#8212; are the reasons I founded Human Value Exchange.</p><p>Adam&#8217;s emphasis on community as the ultimate amplifier resonates most: &#8220;Without this amazing community, I would be nowhere.&#8221; He&#8217;s spot-on. In a decentralized world, there&#8217;s no 1-800 help desk &#8212; we rely on plebs sharpening plebs. Bitcoin Well supports this by making non-custodial access seamless, while we at Human Value Exchange focus on the transition to a new value system. Adam has definitely inspired me to re-start my connection with the local Bitcoin community via meet ups.</p><p>What communities need to do right now is set up a bitcoin circular economy. With the immanent death of the central banking fiat slave system, merchants and communities need to be building a real-world Bitcoin utility.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RhAh!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd7385c2a-7d82-43c6-bbbd-4ffd773bcbbb_1384x1009.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!RhAh!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd7385c2a-7d82-43c6-bbbd-4ffd773bcbbb